diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index c9415f9..dd00ed0 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -107,6 +107,16 @@ Only `id`, one of `path` or `path_prefix`, and `upstreams` are required; the val
 may not touch hop-by-hop fields, `Host`, `Content-Length`, `Trailer` or the headers the gateway
 owns (`X-Request-Id`, `X-Forwarded-For`, `-Proto` and `-Host`, `X-Consumer-Id`).
 
+A route may also set a `tls` object for how the gateway connects to its upstreams, which must then
+all be `https` URLs (a route with `tls` and a plain `http` upstream fails the load): `ca_file` is
+the CA that signs their certificates (the system roots are not used when it is set), `cert_file` and
+`key_file` are the client certificate the gateway presents to them (set together), `server_name` the
+name it expects in their certificates, and `min_version` is `"1.2"` (the default) or `"1.3"`. The
+files are read when the routes are loaded, and by `check-routes`, so a broken file fails the load
+and a reload picks up a rotated certificate. Health checks of the route use the same settings.
+Routes with equal settings share one transport; after a reload, the first request on a TLS route
+closes the idle connections of the transports no route uses any more.
+
 Every problem is reported with the route and field, for example
 `route "orders": retry.attempts: must be between 1 and 10, got 11`. Check a file without starting
 the gateway:
